<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="AARCH64:LE:64:v8A:default">
<!--
    Data imports read through an import slot (`option importdata on|off`).

    Issue: a data import is reached through a slot the dynamic loader fills
    with the import's address, `ldr x8,[slot]; ldr w8,[x8]`. kuna names that
    slot for the import and paints it externref, which is how a CALL through it
    deindirects to the import; a DATA read is not a call, so it printed as a
    dereference of the anonymous slot. On the A13 trustd that is 921 reads,
    `if (*dat_1041cc6c8 == ...)` for the stack-protector guard on Toyota.

    Stage / sub-stage: P9 naming-policy, `PrintC::op_load`
    (`kuna-decomp/src/p9_emit/printc.rs`, `import_slot_name`), resolved as
    ActionDeindirect resolves a call through the same slot.

    P0 assertion: `option importdata on|off` (default off). It is read when C is
    printed; `clear architecture` resets it, so pass 2 sets it after its load.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. Both passes clear
    it and load the real arm64 Mach-O fixture `macho_gotdata` (built from
    `macho_gotdata.c`, see the fixtures README): `_main` @0x100000448 reads
    `imported_counter` and `imported_name` through their `__DATA_CONST,__got`
    slots @0x100004000 and @0x100004008.

    Pass 1 (the default, the BUG): the reads are `*dat_100004000` and
    `*dat_100004008`. Pass 2 (`option importdata on`, the FIX): they are
    `imported_counter` and `imported_name`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_gotdata</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x100000448</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_gotdata</com>
  <com>option importdata on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x100000448</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="importdata off: the imported counter is read through its __got slot" min="1" max="1">v1 = \*dat_100004000;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="importdata off: the imported pointer is tested through its __got slot" min="1" max="1">if \(\*dat_100004008\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="importdata on: the imported counter renders as the import" min="1" max="1">v1 = imported_counter;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="importdata on: the imported pointer renders as the import" min="1" max="1">if \(imported_name\)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
